1
00:00:00,810 --> 00:00:04,030
How does a simulated experience
become a useful finding?

2
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:08,590
Inside Gnomi, a product experiment
becomes a sequence you can inspect:

3
00:00:08,810 --> 00:00:11,990
what each persona saw, did, and heard.

4
00:00:12,490 --> 00:00:14,350
Start by defining the experiment.

5
00:00:14,570 --> 00:00:18,790
Freeze the question, population,
product version, outcomes,

6
00:00:18,890 --> 00:00:20,310
and limits.

7
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:25,350
For an A/B comparison, use matched
populations and networks, with

8
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:27,790
separate mutable state in each world.

9
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:30,030
The population is synthetic.

10
00:00:30,410 --> 00:00:34,710
Each persona brings goals,
familiarity, constraints, and prior

11
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:35,830
experience.

12
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:39,030
A directed network defines who follows whom.

13
00:00:39,370 --> 00:00:43,345
These are explicit modeling assumptions;
adding more personas does not

14
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:45,310
remove shared model bias.

15
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:48,070
The simulation lives in its own runtime.

16
00:00:48,410 --> 00:00:50,950
The app presents controls and results.

17
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:53,670
The engine handles authoring and imports.

18
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:57,745
Adapters connect the runtime to
browsers, model providers, and

19
00:00:57,770 --> 00:01:00,830
storage, so the same
core can run headlessly.

20
00:01:01,290 --> 00:01:03,910
Execution moves through logical rounds.

21
00:01:04,170 --> 00:01:06,830
First, personas experience the product.

22
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:11,310
Each step combines permitted observations
with that persona's own memory.

23
00:01:11,770 --> 00:01:15,665
Models propose behavior; code
checks valid actions and records

24
00:01:15,690 --> 00:01:16,590
evidence.

25
00:01:16,970 --> 00:01:19,590
Independent personas can work concurrently.

26
00:01:20,090 --> 00:01:24,430
Next, freeze the social snapshot
and select who reads which posts.

27
00:01:24,810 --> 00:01:27,190
Everyone sees only their permitted feed.

28
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:29,990
A quiet reader can still update an opinion.

29
00:01:30,410 --> 00:01:33,745
Forming a first opinion is recorded
separately from changing an existing

30
00:01:33,770 --> 00:01:34,470
one.

31
00:01:34,890 --> 00:01:37,390
Model requests may finish in any order.

32
00:01:37,770 --> 00:01:41,150
Validated decisions are applied
in stable logical order.

33
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:45,710
This keeps a fast API response from
deciding whose post appears newest.

34
00:01:46,090 --> 00:01:48,830
Then the next round starts
from the updated state.

35
00:01:49,290 --> 00:01:51,870
Evidence keeps experience
separate from echo.

36
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:55,985
A persona may discover a problem
firsthand, or report it after hearing

37
00:01:56,010 --> 00:01:57,030
someone else.

38
00:01:57,370 --> 00:01:58,830
Both remain visible.

39
00:01:59,210 --> 00:02:03,185
Firsthand counts drive finding rankings,
while observed or confirmed browser

40
00:02:03,210 --> 00:02:04,710
evidence is retained.

41
00:02:05,130 --> 00:02:08,070
The design distinguishes
three kinds of repeatability.

42
00:02:08,490 --> 00:02:11,110
Event replay rebuilds from saved events.

43
00:02:11,530 --> 00:02:15,750
Recorded-input execution checks that
scheduling changes preserve outcomes.

44
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:19,670
Fresh replicates make new
requests, so outputs can vary.

45
00:02:20,090 --> 00:02:23,630
The dedicated run store and
recovery protocol are planned work.

46
00:02:24,010 --> 00:02:26,630
Efficiency comes from
assigning work carefully.

47
00:02:27,130 --> 00:02:30,630
Code handles selection,
accounting, validation, and

48
00:02:30,810 --> 00:02:31,630
metrics.

49
00:02:32,090 --> 00:02:34,990
Models handle language
and behavioral proposals.

50
00:02:35,370 --> 00:02:39,350
Budgets, retries, and model
settings must stay visible.

51
00:02:39,770 --> 00:02:43,425
Any claimed speedup needs a measured
comparison that also checks behavioral

52
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:44,390
quality.

53
00:02:44,810 --> 00:02:46,705
Evaluation compares whole runs.

54
00:02:46,730 --> 00:02:50,545
Match A and B within each replicate,
then compare differences across

55
00:02:50,570 --> 00:02:51,830
independent pairs.

56
00:02:52,010 --> 00:02:56,305
Test social on versus off, ranking
versus chronological feeds, and

57
00:02:56,330 --> 00:02:57,790
alternative networks.

58
00:02:58,170 --> 00:03:01,590
Connected personas are not
independent human observations.

59
00:03:01,850 --> 00:03:05,665
The runtime, corrected social
rules, and evaluation harness are

60
00:03:05,690 --> 00:03:07,630
implemented on the simulation branch.

61
00:03:07,770 --> 00:03:10,630
Human behavioral validation
has not been done.

62
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:15,505
Gnomi turns synthetic experiences into
traceable hypotheses, helping teams

63
00:03:15,530 --> 00:03:17,750
decide what to investigate with real people.
